{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>For</b> — It has become clear to me the immensity of His greatness; therefore I ask of you that you bless Him and praise Him above all the supernal angels and the inferior elohim, which are the idols. He called them elohim in correspondence to the thoughts of their worshippers, like Hananiah the prophet, and he was a false prophet, and many like this are in Scripture — and the absolute proof of the greatness of HaShem."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 135, :notes {0 "The comment appears to open with an ellipsis or implicit quotation; rendered the abrupt opening as-is."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:41:45.794699196Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}